{"ld": 1286, "paper": "SP515", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, to Establish the Commission to Study the Impact of Blockchain Technology and Cryptocurrency on Maine's Economy and the Risks of Fraud and Theft to Maine Consumers (EMERGENCY) (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "s-bradstreet-richard", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-archer-marshall", "h-collins-alicia", "h-flynn-paul", "h-foley-robert", "s-haggan-david"], "committee_code": "HCIFS", "committee_name": "Health Coverage, Insurance and Financial Services", "summary": {"text": "This resolve establishes the Commission to Study Fostering a Positive Economic Environment for Blockchain Technology and Cryptocurrency. The commission is tasked with reviewing national data on the scope of the use of blockchain technology and cryptocurrency, assessing the current status of blockchain technology and cryptocurrency within the State, studying nonfungible tokens, consulting industry experts and compiling legislative recommendations to position the State as a leader in the emerging fields of blockchain technology and cryptocurrency. The commission is directed to report on its study no later than December 3, 2025 to the Joint Standing Committee on Health Coverage, Insurance and Financial Services, which is authorized to report out legislation based on the report.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0515&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Died On Adjournment", "final_disposition": {"label": "Died On Adjournment", "date": "2026-04-29", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1286)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0515&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-240)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0515&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (S-240)", "d